        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-materials','Within the linear elastic range, what does Young’s modulus represent?','The slope of the stress–strain curve',['The product of stress and strain','The fracture stress only','The permanent strain after unloading'],'In the linear elastic region, E=stress/strain and is the curve slope.','D2','NON_NUMERICAL','elastic-modulus-meaning','material-selection','confuses stiffness with strength or failure stress',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-materials','A conductor’s resistance increases as it is heated, with positive temperature coefficient. Which trend is expected for a fixed voltage source?','Current decreases',['Current increases','Current remains fixed','Resistance becomes zero'],'With V fixed, I=V/R; increasing R reduces current.','D3','CONCEPTUAL_QUANTITATIVE','temperature-resistance-current','thermal-electrical-coupling','assumes fixed voltage fixes current',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-materials','A material returns to its original shape after the load is removed. What behavior does this demonstrate?','Elastic response',['Plastic flow','Creep only','Fracture'],'Elastic deformation is recoverable upon unloading within the material’s elastic range.','D2','NON_NUMERICAL','elastic-recovery','load-unload','treats all deformation as permanent',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-materials','A 2 m rod has α=10×10⁻⁶/°C and warms by 30°C. What length increase is predicted?','0.6 mm',['6 mm','0.06 mm','60 mm'],'ΔL=αLΔT=10×10⁻⁶(2)(30)=0.0006 m=0.6 mm.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','thermal-expansion','temperature-change','misses the micro-prefix conversion','10e-6*2*30=.0006m'),
