        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-materials','A material shows a large strain after a small stress increase near failure. What is the most relevant concern?','Reduced stiffness or impending instability/damage, depending on the material response',['Higher Young’s modulus by definition','Guaranteed elastic recovery','No change in deformation'],'A steep increase in strain for little added stress signals reduced tangent stiffness and requires evaluation of the failure mode.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','nonlinear-material-response','failure-interpretation','assumes stress–strain response remains linear through failure',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-materials','For the same material and length, doubling conductor cross-sectional area does what to its ideal resistance?','Halves it',['Doubles it','Leaves it unchanged','Quadruples it'],'R=ρL/A, so doubling A halves R.','D3','CONCEPTUAL_QUANTITATIVE','area-resistance-inverse','conductor-sizing-principle','assumes resistance is proportional to area',''),
