        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-thermodynamics','Why does insulation reduce heat loss through a wall?','It adds thermal resistance to the heat-flow path',['It increases the temperature difference','It creates energy','It eliminates all convection everywhere'],'Insulation increases resistance, reducing heat flow for a given temperature difference.','D2','NON_NUMERICAL','thermal-resistance','building-thermal-path','confuses thermal resistance with temperature difference',''),
