        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-electronics-semiconductor','An ideal diode is reverse biased below breakdown. What is its approximate current in the ideal model?','Zero',['Infinite','Equal to forward current','Set by the source voltage alone'],'The ideal reverse-biased diode is an open circuit until breakdown.','D2','NON_NUMERICAL','ideal-diode-reverse-state','rectifier-model','treats reverse bias as short circuit',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-safety-code','A worker must test a circuit after isolation. Why should the tester be checked before and after the test?','To confirm the instrument functioned during the absence-of-voltage check',['To calibrate the circuit breaker','To prove the tag has legal force','To raise the circuit voltage'],'A prove-test-prove sequence helps establish that the tester was operational before and after the measurement.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','tester-prove-test-prove','electrical-isolation','treats a failed tester indication as proof of zero voltage',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-safety-code','A damaged cable is found in a shared work area. What is the immediate risk-control priority?','Prevent contact and arrange isolation/qualified assessment',['Continue using it at lower load','Tape over the damage while energized','Wait for routine maintenance'],'Restrict access and control the energy source before repair; do not rely on an improvised energized repair.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','damaged-cable-control','site-hazard','reduces load instead of controlling exposure',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-safety-code','A safety procedure requires PPE but the work area remains energized and uncontrolled. What is the correct assessment?','PPE does not replace feasible hazard elimination or isolation',['PPE makes every energized task safe','Hazard controls are optional once PPE is worn','Only warning signs are required'],'PPE is a final protective layer, not a substitute for practicable source control and safe-work planning.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','hierarchy-of-controls','work-planning','treats PPE as the sole control',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-safety-code','A risk assessment identifies a credible arc hazard. Which information should guide the control plan?','Task conditions, equipment state, exposure, and qualified hazard assessment',['Only the equipment color','A generic PPE list without task details','The worker’s years of service alone'],'Risk controls must match the actual task, equipment, energy state, and exposure; unsupported numerical limits are not inferred.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','task-specific-risk-assessment','electrical-work-planning','uses generic controls without hazard analysis',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-safety-code','Why should a worker stop and report an unexpected voltage indication after isolation?','The assumed safe state is not verified',['The meter reading can always be ignored','A tag overrides the measured indication','Unexpected voltage proves the instrument is calibrated'],'Unexpected voltage is evidence that isolation or measurement assumptions need investigation before work proceeds.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','unexpected-voltage-response','isolation-verification','trusts an administrative assumption over field evidence',''),
