        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-chemistry','A galvanic cell produces electrical energy from a spontaneous chemical reaction. Which statement describes electron flow in its external circuit?','Electrons move from anode toward cathode',['Electrons move from cathode to anode through the electrolyte only','Electrons do not move','Positive ions carry all external-circuit current'],'Oxidation at the anode releases electrons that travel through the external circuit to the cathode.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','galvanic-electron-path','electrochemical-conversion','reverses anode and cathode roles',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-chemistry','A sample has 0.5 mol of a substance with molar mass 40 g/mol. What is its mass?','20 g',['80 g','0.0125 g','40.5 g'],'m=nM=0.5(40)=20 g.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','mole-mass-conversion','chemical-quantity','divides molar mass by amount','0.5*40=20g'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-chemistry','A salt dissolves into ions in water. Why can the solution conduct electricity better than the pure solvent?','The ions are mobile charge carriers',['The ions prevent charge motion','The solvent becomes a metal','The salt removes all electric fields'],'Dissolved ions carry charge through the liquid under an electric field.','D2','NON_NUMERICAL','electrolyte-conduction','solution-properties','assumes molecular dissolution removes charge carriers',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-chemistry','A reaction releases heat to its surroundings. Under the usual chemistry sign convention, what is the sign of system heat q?','Negative',['Positive','Zero','Undefined for a reaction'],'Heat leaving the system is q<0 under the stated convention.','D2','NON_NUMERICAL','thermochemical-sign','reaction-energy','confuses surroundings receiving heat with system absorbing it',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-chemistry','A solution changes from pH 6 to pH 4. By what factor does hydrogen-ion concentration change?','It becomes 100 times greater',['It becomes 2 times greater','It becomes 100 times smaller','It remains unchanged'],'A two-unit decrease on the logarithmic pH scale means 10² increase in hydrogen-ion concentration.','D3','CONCEPTUAL_QUANTITATIVE','ph-logarithmic-change','solution-acidity','treats a pH difference as a linear concentration change','10^(6-4)=100'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-chemistry','In a balanced chemical equation, what is conserved across reactants and products?','The number of atoms of each element',['The number of molecules in every case','The physical state of each substance','The reaction rate'],'Balancing enforces atom conservation for each element; molecule count may change.','D2','NON_NUMERICAL','chemical-equation-balance','reaction-stoichiometry','assumes molecule counts must be equal',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-chemistry','A metal is selected for a wet environment. Which property most directly helps resist electrochemical attack?','Corrosion resistance in the expected environment',['High density alone','Low melting point','High electrical resistance only'],'Material selection should consider corrosion behavior in the actual chemical and moisture environment.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','corrosion-material-selection','environmental-durability','selects from unrelated bulk property alone',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-law-code-ethics','An engineer is asked to approve a design after discovering a material assumption outside their expertise. What should they do?','Obtain competent review and clearly limit any certification',['Approve because the client accepts risk','Sign and add a private note later','Copy another engineer’s seal'],'A professional may not imply competence or verification that did not occur; qualified review and transparent limits are required.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','competence-and-certification','professional-accountability','treats client waiver as a substitute for competence',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-law-code-ethics','A supervisor directs an engineer to omit a known design limitation from a report. What is the ethical response?','Retain material limitations and refuse a misleading report',['Remove the limitation to protect schedule','Mention it only verbally','Delete the supporting calculation'],'Professional communications should be accurate and not materially misleading.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','complete-technical-disclosure','reporting-integrity','treats omission as harmless when conclusion is favorable',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-law-code-ethics','A practitioner receives confidential client data. When may it be disclosed?','When authorized or legally required, with proper safeguards',['Whenever a colleague is curious','Whenever it would improve publicity','Never, even if a lawful safety disclosure is required'],'Confidentiality is important but is subject to authorization and applicable legal or professional duties.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','confidentiality-duty','client-information','assumes confidentiality has no lawful exceptions',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-law-code-ethics','An engineer signs a calculation prepared by a junior colleague. What must be true for responsible approval?','The engineer has reviewed it adequately and accepts professional responsibility',['The junior has a higher GPA','The calculation contains no units','The client has already paid'],'A signature should reflect meaningful review and responsibility, not mere administrative routing.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','responsible-supervision','design-review','confuses delegation with transfer of accountability',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-law-code-ethics','A proposed shortcut could expose the public to an unassessed hazard. Which duty is paramount?','Protect public welfare and communicate the risk',['Protect the schedule first','Avoid raising concerns in writing','Defer to whoever pays the invoice'],'Public protection is a controlling professional obligation when safety risk is credible.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','public-welfare-duty','risk-escalation','subordinates safety to commercial pressure',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-law-code-ethics','A practitioner’s registration status is relevant to a regulated professional act. What is the responsible first check?','Verify current authorization through the proper official channel',['Assume a prior card remains valid forever','Rely on a social-media profile','Use another person’s credentials'],'Current professional authorization should be verified from official records when it affects the act.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','license-status-verification','regulated-practice','treats old credentials as proof of current status',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-law-code-ethics','A technical opinion is requested outside the evidence available. What should the engineer communicate?','The limits of evidence and what additional information is needed',['A definitive conclusion anyway','Only the preferred answer','A fabricated missing measurement'],'Professional advice should distinguish known facts, assumptions, and unresolved evidence.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','evidence-limit-disclosure','technical-opinion','converts uncertainty into unsupported certainty',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-law-code-ethics','Two engineers disagree about a calculation. What is the most professional way to resolve it?','Compare assumptions, governing method, and reproducible steps',['Choose the more senior person automatically','Average the two answers without analysis','Suppress the disagreement'],'Transparent technical review can locate differences in assumptions, method, units, or arithmetic.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','reproducible-peer-review','engineering-disagreement','uses hierarchy rather than technical evidence',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-law-code-ethics','A report includes a safety recommendation based on an assumption not yet tested. How should it be presented?','Label it as conditional and identify the needed verification',['State it as an observed fact','Remove the assumption from the record','Call it code-mandated without a source'],'Separate observed evidence from conditional assumptions so the reader can judge the recommendation.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','assumption-qualification','professional-reporting','presents an unverified assumption as fact',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-contracts-specifications','A specification sets a minimum insulation class and a vendor offers a higher class with documented compatibility. What is needed before acceptance?','Verify every stated requirement and obtain authorized approval for substitution',['Accept automatically because higher is always better','Reject all substitutions regardless of evidence','Ignore compatibility because class is higher'],'A higher rating does not by itself prove interface, compatibility, or contractual acceptance.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','substitution-conformance','technical-submittal','assumes one superior rating satisfies all requirements',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-contracts-specifications','A drawing and written specification conflict. What should the reviewer do?','Resolve the discrepancy through the contract’s formal clarification process',['Choose whichever is easier to build','Ignore both and rely on memory','Let the installer decide silently'],'Conflicting contract documents require an authorized clarification rather than unilateral assumptions.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','document-conflict-resolution','design-coordination','uses informal preference to resolve a material conflict',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-contracts-specifications','A test report gives a result but no instrument calibration status. What is the concern?','The measurement’s traceability and validity are not established',['The result must be exact','Calibration status affects only document color','The measurement automatically passes'],'Measurement acceptance needs suitable instrument status and a traceable test record.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','test-record-validity','quality-documentation','treats a numerical result as self-validating',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-contracts-specifications','A scope change affects cost and completion time. What record best supports the decision?','A reviewed, authorized change document describing scope, price, and schedule effects',['An unsigned text message only','A revised invoice with no technical basis','A verbal instruction remembered later'],'A controlled change record preserves the technical change and its authorized commercial and schedule consequences.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','change-control-record','project-documentation','confuses informal notice with approved change',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-contracts-specifications','A specification uses the word “shall” for a test requirement. How should it be interpreted in a compliance review?','As a stated mandatory requirement unless the governing document defines otherwise',['As an optional suggestion','As a warranty period','As proof the test already passed'],'The reviewer should apply the contract’s defined terminology and treat “shall” as a requirement in ordinary specification usage.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','requirement-language','specification-interpretation','reads mandatory language as a recommendation',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-computer-programming','A list has n values. What is the index of its first element in a zero-based language?','0',['1','n','−1'],'Zero-based indexing begins at index zero.','D2','CONCEPTUAL_QUANTITATIVE','zero-based-first-index','array-processing','assumes one-based indexing','first index = 0'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-computer-programming','A repeated calculation must stop when the change between successive estimates is below tolerance. What is this criterion?','A convergence condition',['A syntax rule','A data type','A sorting key'],'An iterative method stops when its error or change criterion meets a specified tolerance.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','iterative-convergence-test','numerical-software','stops after arbitrary iterations without checking convergence',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-computer-programming','A function changes a shared array unexpectedly. Which debugging step is most useful first?','Trace references and side effects at the function boundary',['Increase the array size','Disable all tests','Change the output units'],'Shared mutable references can allow side effects; inspect ownership, inputs, and writes.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','state-side-effect-tracing','software-debugging','assumes a wrong output is necessarily an arithmetic error',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-computer-programming','A numerical routine accepts NaN as a valid sensor value and propagates it. What check is missing?','Finite-value validation',['Loop unrolling','Sorting','Comment formatting'],'Reject or explicitly handle non-finite values before downstream arithmetic.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','nonfinite-data-validation','measurement-software','assumes a numeric data type guarantees a finite value',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-computer-programming','A routine uses a nested loop over n records in both dimensions. What is its dominant operation growth?','O(n²)',['O(n)','O(log n)','O(1)'],'The n-by-n iteration performs work proportional to n².','D3','CONCEPTUAL_QUANTITATIVE','quadratic-loop-growth','algorithm-analysis','counts only one loop dimension',''),
