        b638_q('b633-ree-math-fourier-laplace','What is the Laplace transform of the derivative x′(t), including initial value x(0−)?','sX(s)−x(0−)',['X(s)/s','sX(s)+x(0−)','X(s)−s'],'Integration by parts yields L{x′}=sX−x(0−).','D4','CONCEPTUAL_QUANTITATIVE','derivative-transform-initial-condition','initial-value-model','drops or reverses the initial-condition term',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-math-fourier-laplace','A Fourier spectrum has a strong component at 60 Hz and a smaller one at 180 Hz. What is the frequency relationship?','The smaller component is the third harmonic of 60 Hz',['It is the second harmonic','It is a subharmonic','It is unrelated to the fundamental'],'180/60=3, so 180 Hz is the third harmonic.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','harmonic-order-identification','spectrum-interpretation','counts the fundamental as harmonic zero','180/60=3'),
        // Allied sciences: varied physical models and evidence interpretation.
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-mechanics','A 20 N force acts at 30° above horizontal. What is its horizontal component?','10√3 N',['10 N','20√3 N','20 N'],'The horizontal component is 20 cos30°=10√3 N.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','oblique-force-component','force-resolution','uses sine for the adjacent horizontal component','20*cos(30deg)=10sqrt3N'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-mechanics','A body moves at constant velocity on a level surface. What is the net force?','Zero',['Equal to its weight','Equal to friction','Increasing with time'],'Zero acceleration implies zero resultant force by Newton’s second law.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','constant-velocity-resultant','motion-diagnosis','assumes motion requires a continuing net force',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-mechanics','A 2 kg object changes speed from 3 to 7 m/s. What is its change in kinetic energy?','40 J',['20 J','28 J','98 J'],'ΔK=½m(v₂²−v₁²)=1(49−9)=40 J.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','kinetic-energy-change','energy-accounting','uses the speed difference instead of the squared-speed difference','0.5*2*(49-9)=40J'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-mechanics','A force is perpendicular to a body’s instantaneous displacement. What work does that force do?','Zero',['Positive maximum work','Negative maximum work','Force times elapsed time'],'Work is F·s=Fs cos90°=0.','D3','CONCEPTUAL_QUANTITATIVE','perpendicular-force-work','energy-transfer','equates any nonzero force with nonzero work',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-mechanics','A 0.4 kg mass rotates at 5 rad/s on a 0.2 m radius. What is centripetal acceleration?','5 m/s²',['1 m/s²','10 m/s²','25 m/s²'],'aᶜ=rω²=0.2(25)=5 m/s².','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','angular-speed-centripetal-acceleration','rotational-motion','uses angular speed without squaring it','0.2*5^2=5m/s^2'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-mechanics','Two equal and opposite forces act along different parallel lines. What is their combined mechanical effect?','A couple producing rotation',['A single zero-moment force','A net translational force','No effect in every case'],'The resultant force is zero but the separated lines of action create a nonzero couple moment.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','force-couple-resultant','rotational-equilibrium','looks only at force sum and ignores moment arm',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-mechanics','A 100 N load is supported equally by two vertical members. What idealized axial force does each carry?','50 N compression',['100 N compression each','50 N tension','25 N compression'],'Under equal symmetric sharing, each member carries half the total load in compression.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','symmetric-load-sharing','support-reaction','assigns the full applied load to each support','100/2=50N'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-materials','A metal specimen returns to its original shape after unloading. The deformation was primarily what?','Elastic',['Plastic','Fracture','Creep only'],'Recoverable deformation is elastic; permanent set indicates plastic deformation.','D2','NON_NUMERICAL','elastic-recovery','material-response','equates any deformation with permanent yielding',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-materials','A bar has E=200 GPa, stress=100 MPa, and remains linear-elastic. What is the axial strain?','0.0005',['0.5','0.002','2,000'],'ε=σ/E=100×10⁶/(200×10⁹)=0.0005.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','hooke-law-strain','elastic-design-estimate','fails to convert MPa and GPa consistently','100e6/200e9=.0005'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-materials','A brittle ceramic has high compressive strength but low tensile strength. Which loading concern is especially important?','Avoiding tensile stress concentrations',['Increasing compressive stress at all costs','Ignoring cracks under tension','Assuming it yields plastically first'],'Brittle materials are sensitive to tensile flaws and crack propagation.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','brittle-tensile-fracture','material-selection','uses compressive strength as proof of tensile toughness',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-materials','Two materials have equal dimensions and are heated by the same ΔT. Which expands more freely?','The one with the larger coefficient of thermal expansion',['The one with the larger elastic modulus always','The one with greater density always','Neither can expand'],'Free thermal strain is αΔT, so the larger α produces more expansion.','D3','CONCEPTUAL_QUANTITATIVE','thermal-expansion-comparison','thermal-clearance','confuses stiffness with free thermal strain',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-materials','A material is subjected to repeated stress below its one-cycle yield strength. What failure mechanism may still occur?','Fatigue',['Creep only at room temperature','No failure is possible','Instantaneous ductile overload'],'Repeated cycles can initiate and grow fatigue cracks even below monotonic yield stress.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','cyclic-fatigue-risk','service-life-assessment','assumes below-yield means unlimited cyclic life',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-materials','A test coupon elongates 2 mm over a 1 m gauge length. What engineering strain is measured?','0.002',['0.02','2','500'],'Engineering strain is ΔL/L₀=0.002/1=0.002.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','engineering-strain-measurement','materials-testing','uses elongation alone without normalizing by gauge length','.002/1=.002'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-thermodynamics','A closed system receives 500 J of heat and performs 200 J of work. What is its internal-energy change?','+300 J',['+700 J','−300 J','−700 J'],'Using ΔU=Q−W with work done by the system positive gives 500−200=300 J.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','first-law-closed-system','energy-balance','adds work done by the system to heat input','500-200=300J'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-thermodynamics','A refrigerator removes heat from a cold space and rejects it to a warmer room. What must be supplied?','Work input',['No energy input','Only cold air','A lower-temperature sink'],'Heat transfer from cold to hot requires external work in the refrigeration cycle.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','refrigeration-work-direction','thermal-system','treats a refrigerator as spontaneous reverse heat flow',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-thermodynamics','A 500 W heater operates for 20 minutes. How much energy does it use?','600 kJ',['10 kJ','6 kJ','1,000 kJ'],'Time is 1,200 s; E=Pt=500×1,200=600,000 J=600 kJ.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','power-time-energy-conversion','thermal-load','uses minutes as seconds without conversion','500*20*60=600000J'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-thermodynamics','Two bodies reach thermal equilibrium in an insulated enclosure. What is true at equilibrium?','They have the same temperature and no net heat transfer between them',['They contain equal internal energy','They have equal mass','Each has zero energy'],'Thermal equilibrium equalizes temperature and removes net heat flow; stored energy need not be equal.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','thermal-equilibrium-condition','heat-exchange','confuses equal temperature with equal energy',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-thermodynamics','A 0.5 kg sample with c=400 J/(kg·K) is warmed by 10 K. How much sensible heat is absorbed?','2,000 J',['200 J','4,000 J','20,000 J'],'Q=mcΔT=0.5(400)(10)=2,000 J.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','specific-heat-energy','thermal-storage','omits the sample mass','0.5*400*10=2000J'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-thermodynamics','A heat exchanger has a fouled surface. What trend is most likely for heat transfer at fixed geometry and conditions?','Reduced heat-transfer rate',['Increased heat transfer due to insulation','No possible change','A reversal of heat-flow direction'],'Fouling adds thermal resistance and generally reduces transfer for the same driving temperature difference.','D4','CONCEPTUAL_QUANTITATIVE','fouling-thermal-resistance','equipment-performance','assumes added resistance improves heat transfer',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-fluid-mechanics','A 0.8 m³ volume of water has approximate mass 800 kg. What density does this imply?','1,000 kg/m³',['640 kg/m³','0.001 kg/m³','1.6 kg/m³'],'Density is m/V=800/0.8=1,000 kg/m³.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','density-from-mass-volume','fluid-property','multiplies mass and volume','800/.8=1000kg/m^3'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-fluid-mechanics','At a submerged point, how does static pressure change with depth in a uniform-density fluid?','It increases linearly with depth',['It decreases linearly','It is independent of depth','It increases with the square of depth'],'Hydrostatic gauge pressure is ρgh for constant density and gravitational acceleration.','D3','CONCEPTUAL_QUANTITATIVE','hydrostatic-depth-trend','tank-pressure','confuses pressure with fluid velocity',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-fluid-mechanics','A pipe area contracts to one-third while incompressible steady flow rate is maintained. What happens to mean velocity?','It triples',['It becomes one-third','It is unchanged','It becomes nine times as large'],'Continuity Q=Av requires velocity to rise by a factor of three.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','continuity-area-ratio','conduit-flow','keeps velocity constant despite conserved flow rate','A2=A1/3;v2=3v1'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-fluid-mechanics','A pump adds energy to a flowing fluid. Which equation form should account for that input?','An extended energy equation with pump head',['Bernoulli equation with no added head or losses','A mass balance only','The ideal-gas law only'],'A pump adds head; real systems may also require turbine, friction, and minor-loss terms.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','pump-head-energy-balance','hydraulic-system','applies an ideal no-work equation across a pump',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-fluid-mechanics','A manometer fluid is denser than the measured liquid. For the same pressure difference, its required height difference is generally what?','Smaller',['Larger','Identical for all densities','Zero'],'Hydrostatic balance Δp=ρgΔh gives a smaller height difference for greater density.','D4','CONCEPTUAL_QUANTITATIVE','manometer-density-height','pressure-measurement','assumes column height is independent of fluid density',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-fluid-mechanics','A hydraulic press has input piston area 0.01 m² and output area 0.2 m². Ideally, what force multiplication occurs?','20 times',['0.05 times','2 times','200 times'],'Equal pressure gives Fout/Fin=Aout/Ain=0.2/0.01=20.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','hydraulic-force-ratio','force-amplification','uses the inverse area ratio','.2/.01=20'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-electronics-semiconductor','A diode is forward biased in its normal operating range. Which carrier motion supports conduction?','Majority carriers cross the junction barrier',['Only minority carriers move and majority carriers stop','The depletion region becomes infinitely wide','The device stores no charge in any condition'],'Forward bias lowers the junction barrier and allows substantial majority-carrier injection.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','pn-forward-bias-carriers','device-operation','reverses forward and reverse bias behavior',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-electronics-semiconductor','A transistor is used as a switch and driven into saturation. Which idealized state applies?','Both junctions are forward-biased in the basic BJT model',['Both junctions are reverse-biased','Collector current is exactly zero','It is necessarily in the active linear region'],'In the basic NPN BJT model, saturation forward-biases both base-emitter and base-collector junctions.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','bjt-saturation-junctions','switching-device','confuses cutoff or active region with saturation',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-electronics-semiconductor','A silicon diode model uses a 0.7 V forward drop. At 10 mA, what is its approximate dissipation?','7 mW',['0.7 mW','70 mW','14 mW'],'P=VI=0.7(0.010)=0.007 W=7 mW.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','diode-power-estimate','device-rating','uses milliamperes as amperes','.7*.01=.007W'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-electronics-semiconductor','A reverse-biased diode is below breakdown. What is its idealized current?','Approximately zero except for small leakage',['Large forward current','Exactly the rated surge current','A current proportional to forward voltage'],'The ideal reverse-bias model blocks current; a real diode has small leakage until breakdown.','D2','CONCEPTUAL_QUANTITATIVE','reverse-bias-blocking','rectifier-state','treats reverse bias as forward conduction',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-electronics-semiconductor','A MOSFET gate is insulated from the channel by an oxide. What is the key static input property?','Very high input resistance',['A permanent short to drain','A low-resistance gate junction in every mode','No electric-field control'],'The insulated gate draws negligible steady-state current in the ideal model, though capacitance matters dynamically.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','mosfet-insulated-gate','device-selection','confuses transient gate charging current with steady DC gate current',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-electronics-semiconductor','A transistor junction overheats after power dissipation doubles. Which first-order quantity relates electrical power and thermal rise?','Thermal resistance from junction to reference ambient',['Current gain alone','Gate threshold alone','The clock frequency only'],'A first-order rise estimate is ΔT≈P·Rθ for the relevant thermal path and steady conditions.','D4','CONCEPTUAL_QUANTITATIVE','junction-thermal-path','device-thermal-design','assumes electrical gain alone sets temperature',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-electronics-analog','An inverting op-amp has Rin=10 kΩ and Rf=50 kΩ. What is its ideal voltage gain?','−5',['+5','−0.2','+0.2'],'The ideal inverting gain is −Rf/Rin=−50/10=−5.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','inverting-amplifier-gain','analog-signal-conditioning','drops the inversion sign','-50/10=-5'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-electronics-analog','An ideal non-inverting amplifier has Rf=30 kΩ and Rg=10 kΩ. What is its gain?','4',['3','−3','0.25'],'Gain is 1+Rf/Rg=1+3=4.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','noninverting-amplifier-gain','sensor-amplification','uses the inverting formula','1+30/10=4'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-electronics-analog','An amplifier clips only the positive peaks of a sine input. Which limitation is most directly indicated?','Insufficient positive output swing or bias headroom',['Excessive input resistance','Perfect linearity','An ideal infinite bandwidth'],'Asymmetric clipping indicates the output reached a positive rail or the operating point lacks headroom.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','asymmetric-clipping-diagnosis','waveform-quality','attributes output saturation to input impedance without evidence',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-electronics-analog','A first-order low-pass has R=1 kΩ and C=1 μF. What is its approximate cutoff frequency?','159 Hz',['1.59 kHz','1 Hz','6.28 kHz'],'fc=1/(2πRC)=1/(2π·0.001)≈159 Hz.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','rc-lowpass-cutoff','filter-selection','uses 2πRC instead of its reciprocal','1/(2*pi*1000*1e-6)=159.15Hz'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-electronics-analog','A common-emitter amplifier output is inverted relative to its input. What phase relation is typical in its midband small-signal model?','Approximately 180°',['0°','90°','270° leading only'],'A common-emitter voltage stage produces an inverting midband voltage gain.','D3','CONCEPTUAL_QUANTITATIVE','common-emitter-phase','amplifier-interpretation','assumes every transistor stage is non-inverting',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-electronics-analog','An amplifier has gain 20. What is its voltage gain in decibels?','About 26 dB',['13 dB','20 dB','40 dB'],'Voltage gain in dB is 20log₁₀(20)≈26 dB.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','voltage-gain-decibel','gain-interpretation','uses the power-ratio factor of 10 for voltage ratio','20*log10(20)=26.02dB'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-electronics-digital','An ideal 8-bit unsigned ADC has how many distinct output codes?','256',['8','255','512'],'There are 2⁸=256 codes, numbered 0 through 255.','D2','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','adc-code-count','data-conversion','confuses bit count with code count','2^8=256'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-electronics-digital','A 10-bit unipolar converter spans 0 to 10 V using 2¹⁰ codes. What is the nominal code width using full-scale/code-count?','About 9.77 mV',['10 mV exactly','0.977 V','102.4 mV'],'10 V/1024≈0.00977 V per code under the stated convention.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','adc-quantization-step','measurement-resolution','divides by bits instead of number of codes','10/1024=.009765625V'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-electronics-digital','A sample rate is 12 ksample/s. Under ideal Nyquist conditions, what highest sinusoidal frequency can be represented without aliasing?','Below 6 kHz',['12 kHz','24 kHz','Exactly 6 kHz with no filter assumptions'],'Nyquist requires sampling above twice the highest frequency; the ideal boundary is 6 kHz and practical systems need margin/filtering.','D3','CONCEPTUAL_QUANTITATIVE','sampling-nyquist-boundary','signal-acquisition','uses sample rate itself as maximum signal frequency',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-electronics-digital','A binary word changes from 0111 to 1000. How many bits toggle?','Four',['One','Three','Eight'],'All four bit positions change in this transition.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','binary-transition-hamming-distance','digital-switching','counts numeric increment rather than bit changes','popcount(0111 XOR 1000)=popcount(1111)=4'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-electronics-digital','A parity bit makes the total number of ones even. What does an even-parity check detect?','Any odd number of bit flips',['Every possible burst error','All two-bit errors','The location of an error'],'An odd number of flips changes parity, but even-numbered changes can escape detection and location is not identified.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','parity-detection-limit','data-integrity','assumes parity corrects or locates errors',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-electronics-digital','A 4-bit two’s-complement value is 1110. What signed decimal value does it represent?','−2',['14','−1','−8'],'Invert 1110 to 0001, add one to get magnitude 0010; the sign bit is negative, so value is −2.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','twos-complement-decode','signed-data','reads a signed word as unsigned','1110_2=-2'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-electronics-digital','A logic output is intended to drive a capacitive input. Why can a buffer help?','It supplies drive while isolating the preceding logic node',['It increases the ADC bit depth','It removes all propagation delay','It changes the Boolean function arbitrarily'],'A buffer reduces loading on the source and provides a stronger drive path, though delay remains finite.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','logic-buffer-loading','digital-interface','equates buffering with zero delay',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-instrumentation','A voltage reading fluctuates with a stable DC source. What measurement check should precede replacing the source?','Probe contact, grounding, range, and instrument setup',['Assume the source is defective','Increase the display decimal places only','Short the input terminals'],'Setup faults, ground loops, poor contact, or inappropriate range can create apparent instability.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','measurement-chain-diagnosis','instrument-troubleshooting','attributes all observed variation to the device under test',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-instrumentation','A voltmeter with finite input resistance is connected across a high-resistance source. What can happen?','Loading can reduce the measured voltage',['The meter creates an ideal open circuit','The source resistance becomes zero','The measured voltage must increase'],'The meter forms a divider with source resistance, so finite input resistance can load the source.','D3','CONCEPTUAL_QUANTITATIVE','voltmeter-loading','measurement-loading','assumes the instrument never affects the circuit',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-instrumentation','A 4½-digit meter reports 12.345 V. Which statement is safest about accuracy?','Displayed resolution alone does not establish measurement accuracy',['The value is guaranteed accurate to 1 mV','More digits guarantee lower uncertainty','Calibration is irrelevant'],'Digit count concerns display resolution; accuracy also depends on calibration, range, environment, and uncertainty.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','resolution-versus-accuracy','measurement-uncertainty','equates display digits with accuracy',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-instrumentation','Two independent instruments have standard uncertainties 3 mV and 4 mV. What is their root-sum-square combined uncertainty?','5 mV',['7 mV','1 mV','12 mV'],'For independent uncertainties, √(3²+4²)=5 mV.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','uncertainty-root-sum-square','measurement-combination','adds standard uncertainties linearly without stated dependence','sqrt(3^2+4^2)=5mV'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-instrumentation','A current transformer secondary is energized while its primary current is interrupted. What is the safe general concern?','An open secondary can develop hazardous high voltage; follow approved isolation practice',['The secondary voltage must be zero','The ratio becomes one','Only the polarity marking is affected'],'A CT secondary should not be left open-circuited while primary current flows; use approved shorting and safety procedures.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','ct-open-secondary-hazard','instrument-transformer-safety','treats a current transformer like an open-circuit voltage transformer',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-instrumentation','An instrument reads 49.8 Hz while a reference reads 50.0 Hz. What is the absolute deviation?','0.2 Hz',['0.004 Hz','0.2%','99.8 Hz'],'Absolute deviation is |49.8−50.0|=0.2 Hz.','D2','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','absolute-measurement-deviation','frequency-check','reports the measured value rather than the difference','abs(49.8-50)=.2Hz'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-safety-code','A worker is qualified but lacks task-specific authorization for energized work. What should happen?','Do not proceed; establish authorization and required controls first',['Proceed because qualification alone is sufficient','Ask a bystander to hold the conductor','Use a higher-rated fuse'],'Competence does not replace authorization, risk assessment, isolation, and applicable work controls.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','authorization-before-work','safe-work-planning','confuses qualification with task authorization',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-safety-code','A damaged extension lead has exposed conductors. What is the appropriate action?','Remove it from service and prevent use pending qualified repair or disposal',['Wrap it loosely and continue at full load','Place it under a mat','Use it only when no one is watching'],'Damaged electrical equipment should be isolated from use; improvised concealment preserves the hazard.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','damaged-equipment-withdrawal','portable-equipment-safety','treats visibility reduction as hazard control',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-safety-code','A risk assessment identifies shock and arc hazards. Which control is generally preferred before relying on PPE?','Eliminate or isolate the hazard where practicable',['Rely only on warning labels','Increase work speed','Use ordinary gloves regardless of rating'],'The hierarchy of controls favors eliminating or isolating hazards before administrative controls and PPE.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','electrical-control-hierarchy','hazard-control','treats PPE as the first and only control',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-safety-code','A worker receives an electrical shock but appears able to stand. What is the prudent response?','Activate the emergency response and obtain qualified medical evaluation',['Assume no injury because the worker is standing','Resume work immediately','Give the worker a conductive object'],'Electrical injury can have delayed or internal effects; emergency assessment is prudent after a shock.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','post-shock-response','incident-response','uses visible condition as proof of no injury',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-safety-code','An equipment enclosure is bonded to protective earth. What is the principal purpose?','Provide a low-impedance fault path that supports protective-device operation',['Carry normal load current in every design','Increase touch voltage','Replace insulation'],'Protective bonding limits dangerous potential differences and supports fault clearing when properly designed.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','protective-bonding-purpose','fault-protection','confuses protective conductor function with normal neutral current',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-safety-code','A team changes a switching plan during a job. What should occur before the revised plan is executed?','Pause and review authorization, hazards, isolation, and communication with affected workers',['Continue based on the original briefing','Change labels afterward','Let each worker infer the new sequence'],'A material change requires coordinated review so controls and worker understanding match the actual plan.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','change-control-switching','work-coordination','assumes an earlier briefing covers a changed procedure',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-chemistry','A solution has pH 3. What is its hydrogen-ion concentration under the ideal definition?','10⁻³ mol/L',['3 mol/L','10³ mol/L','10⁻¹¹ mol/L'],'pH=−log₁₀[H⁺], so [H⁺]=10⁻³ mol/L.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','ph-concentration-conversion','electrochemistry','forgets the negative logarithm','[H+]=10^(-pH)=10^-3mol/L'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-chemistry','A redox reaction occurs at an electrode. Oxidation is which process?','Loss of electrons',['Gain of electrons','Gain of protons only','Loss of neutrons'],'Oxidation is electron loss; reduction is electron gain.','D2','NON_NUMERICAL','redox-electron-direction','electrochemical-process','reverses oxidation and reduction',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-chemistry','A galvanic cell operates spontaneously under its conditions. What is the sign of its cell potential?','Positive',['Negative','Exactly zero','Undefined because current flows'],'For a spontaneous galvanic reaction, ΔG=−nFEcell<0, so Ecell is positive.','D3','CONCEPTUAL_QUANTITATIVE','galvanic-potential-sign','cell-operation','reverses the free-energy and potential relationship',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-chemistry','A 2 mol sample contains how many molecules using Avogadro’s number 6.02×10²³ mol⁻¹?','1.204×10²⁴',['3.01×10²³','6.02×10²³','12.04×10²³'],'Multiply amount by Avogadro’s number: 2(6.02×10²³)=1.204×10²⁴.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','mole-particle-count','chemical-quantity','uses molar mass instead of particle count','2*6.02e23=1.204e24'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-chemistry','Why can a salt bridge be important in an electrochemical cell?','It maintains ionic charge balance while limiting direct mixing',['It supplies electrons through the external wire','It stops all ion movement','It makes electrode reactions unnecessary'],'Ion movement through the bridge sustains electroneutrality as electrons travel through the external circuit.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','salt-bridge-charge-balance','cell-architecture','confuses ionic conduction with external electron flow',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-law-code-ethics','An engineer discovers that a signed technical report contains a material error. What is the professional response?','Promptly disclose and correct the error through the responsible process',['Leave it uncorrected if already submitted','Alter the record without notice','Blame the reviewer without evidence'],'Professional integrity requires transparent correction of material technical errors and protection of public interest.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','correction-of-material-error','professional-integrity','treats submission as a reason to conceal a known error',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-law-code-ethics','A current rule is relevant to a design decision, but the source edition cannot be verified. What should the engineer do?','Defer a compliance conclusion until the controlling authority and edition are confirmed',['Assume the newest draft applies','Choose whichever edition is convenient','Cite a review-site summary as binding law'],'Answer-changing legal or code claims require confirmation of the controlling adopted authority; a draft is not automatically effective.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','controlling-edition-verification','code-currentness','treats a proposed revision as effective law',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-law-code-ethics','An engineer is asked to certify work outside the engineer’s demonstrated competence. What is appropriate?','Decline or obtain competent qualified support before certification',['Certify because a deadline exists','Copy another engineer’s signature','Certify with no review'],'Professional responsibility requires competence and a defensible basis for certification.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','competence-boundary','professional-certification','confuses schedule pressure with technical competence',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-law-code-ethics','A client requests that a known safety concern be omitted from a report. What should govern the response?','Public safety and professional obligations, with documented escalation as needed',['The client’s preference alone','The project budget alone','Whether the report is already formatted'],'A professional cannot suppress material safety information merely at a client’s request.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','public-interest-disclosure','ethical-escalation','subordinates public safety to client preference',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-law-code-ethics','A proposed grid-code revision is still under consultation. Which status should be assigned absent a final adoption instrument?','Draft/proposed, not current controlling text',['Automatically effective on publication','Repealed current rule','A universally binding amendment'],'Consultation indicates a proposal; effectiveness requires the applicable final approval/adoption process.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','draft-regulation-status','regulatory-currentness','equates consultation with enactment',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-contracts-specifications','A specification gives a performance requirement and a separate drawing shows one suggested layout. They conflict. What is the first step?','Apply the contract’s order-of-precedence and clarification process',['Silently choose the drawing','Ignore both documents','Change the requirement in the field'],'Contract documents define precedence and change control; a conflict should be resolved through the formal process.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','contract-document-conflict','construction-document-control','treats an illustrative drawing as automatically controlling',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-contracts-specifications','A submittal is marked “reviewed” for general conformity. What does that ordinarily not transfer away from the contractor?','Responsibility for means, methods, and performing the work to contract requirements',['All responsibility for installation','Ownership of the design','The need to verify dimensions'],'Review status does not automatically waive the contractor’s contractual execution obligations.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','submittal-review-responsibility','technical-submittal','interprets review as blanket acceptance of all field work',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-contracts-specifications','A proposed substitution meets nominal voltage but differs in thermal rating and enclosure. What should be compared?','All specified performance, environmental, safety, and interface requirements',['Voltage alone','Brand name alone','Purchase price only'],'A substitution must be evaluated against the complete functional and environmental requirements, not one nameplate value.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','substitution-equivalence-review','equipment-procurement','assumes one matching rating establishes equivalence',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-contracts-specifications','A field instruction changes scope and cost. Which record is needed before treating it as a contractual change?','Authorized written change documentation under the contract',['An informal conversation only','A revised personal timesheet','An unapproved markup'],'Scope, price, and time changes require the contractually authorized change process and documentation.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','authorized-change-record','contract-administration','confuses informal direction with approved variation',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-computer-programming','A loop iterates indices 0 through n−1. How many iterations occur?','n',['n−1','n+1','2n'],'There are n integer indices in the half-open interval [0,n).','D2','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','half-open-loop-count','algorithm-boundary','counts endpoint values as inclusive at n','count=(n-1)-0+1=n'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-computer-programming','A program stores a signed 16-bit two’s-complement integer. What is its representable range?','−32,768 to 32,767',['−65,535 to 65,535','0 to 65,535','−32,767 to 32,768'],'A signed w-bit two’s-complement range is −2^(w−1) to 2^(w−1)−1.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','signed-word-range','embedded-data','uses the unsigned range or makes both endpoints symmetric','-2^15=-32768;2^15-1=32767'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-computer-programming','A routine modifies a shared input array unexpectedly. Which design change reduces this side effect?','Use an explicit copy or immutable interface where appropriate',['Use a global variable','Hide the mutation in a macro','Remove input validation'],'Avoiding unintended mutation makes data flow and behavior easier to reason about.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','side-effect-isolation','software-maintainability','assumes shared mutable state is harmless',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-computer-programming','A sensor sample arrives as an integer in millivolts, but a function expects volts. What is a safe interface strategy?','Convert units explicitly at the boundary and encode/document the unit',['Pass the raw integer without meaning','Rename the variable only','Assume downstream code knows the scale'],'Explicit conversion and unit-bearing interfaces prevent silent factor-of-1,000 errors.','D3','CONCEPTUAL_QUANTITATIVE','unit-boundary-conversion','sensor-interface','treats raw numeric representation as self-describing',''),
        // Professional: lower-heavy leaves are deliberately avoided; focus on smaller pools.
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-generators-conversion','A generator operates at fixed frequency with four poles. What synchronous speed relation applies?','Ns=120f/P',['Ns=60P/f','Ns=fP/120','Ns=120P/f'],'Synchronous speed in rpm is 120f/P; poles increase denominator.','D3','CONCEPTUAL_QUANTITATIVE','synchronous-speed-pole-frequency','machine-speed','reverses pole count and frequency','Ns=120*f/4'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-generators-conversion','A generator terminal voltage falls when lagging load increases. Which effect is a plausible contributor?','Armature reaction and internal impedance drop',['An increase in prime-mover speed must be the only cause','The field flux becomes irrelevant','The load current cannot affect terminal voltage'],'Load-current magnitude and phase affect internal drops and armature reaction, influencing terminal voltage.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','generator-voltage-load-regulation','machine-loading','attributes regulation only to speed change',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-generators-conversion','Two synchronized generators share real load. Which control primarily changes their real-power sharing?','Prime-mover input/governor setpoint',['Field excitation alone','Transformer polarity','Ground-electrode resistance'],'Mechanical input governs real-power contribution, while excitation chiefly affects reactive power and voltage.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','generator-real-reactive-sharing','parallel-generation','swaps governor and excitation roles',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-generators-conversion','A 4-pole synchronous machine runs at 1,800 rpm. What is its frequency?','60 Hz',['30 Hz','120 Hz','7,200 Hz'],'f=PN/120=4(1800)/120=60 Hz.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','machine-frequency-from-speed','frequency-generation','omits the pole-pair relationship','4*1800/120=60Hz'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-power-analysis','A one-line fault model has Thevenin voltage 1 pu and reactance j0.2 pu. What is fault-current magnitude under a bolted-fault model?','5 pu',['0.2 pu','1.2 pu','0.5 pu'],'|I|=|V/Z|=1/0.2=5 pu with the stated simplified model.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','thevenin-fault-current','fault-study','uses reactance as current rather than its reciprocal','1/.2=5pu'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-power-analysis','Per-unit quantities are especially useful when a system includes transformers because they can simplify what?','Comparing quantities across voltage levels on consistent bases',['Eliminating the need for transformer ratio data in every model','Making all losses zero','Replacing protection coordination'],'Consistent bases allow impedance transformations to be represented more simply across voltage levels.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','per-unit-transformer-scaling','system-modeling','believes per-unit removes the need for correct base selection',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-power-analysis','A bus voltage solution is outside the expected range. What should be checked before changing the algorithm?','Units, base values, topology, and input signs',['Only plot colors','The computer clock','The number of report pages'],'Model-data and base inconsistencies often explain implausible outputs before numerical-method changes are warranted.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','load-flow-data-validation','power-system-solution','treats every implausible result as a solver failure',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-power-analysis','A 3-phase short-circuit study uses line voltage 13.8 kV and 100 MVA base. What is the base current?','4.18 kA approximately',['7.25 kA','0.138 kA','13.8 kA'],'Ibase=Sbase/(√3 VLL)=100 MVA/(√3·13.8 kV)≈4.18 kA.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','three-phase-base-current','per-unit-conversion','omits √3 from the line-quantity relation','100e6/(sqrt(3)*13.8e3)=4.18kA'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-wiring-utilization','A load is 2 kW at 0.8 power factor. What is its apparent power?','2.5 kVA',['1.6 kVA','2.0 kVA','3.2 kVA'],'S=P/pf=2/0.8=2.5 kVA.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','real-to-apparent-power','utilization-load','multiplies real power by power factor','2/.8=2.5kVA'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-wiring-utilization','A panel schedule shows a motor starting current above its running current. What design distinction must be respected?','Starting duty and protection coordination versus steady-state loading',['Treat starting current as the continuous operating current automatically','Ignore the starting method','Set every protective device to the highest possible value'],'Starting current is transient and must be assessed with equipment, conductor, and protection requirements rather than confused with continuous load.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','motor-starting-versus-running','motor-utilization','treats an inrush value as continuous demand',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-wiring-utilization','A lighting design has adequate average illuminance but severe glare. What additional aspect requires review?','Luminance distribution, shielding, and viewing geometry',['Only total connected watts','Transformer vector group','Conductor color'],'Average illuminance alone does not describe glare; source luminance and geometry matter.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','lighting-glare-quality','visual-task-design','equates illuminance compliance with visual comfort',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-wiring-utilization','A 1.5 kW load runs for 40 minutes. How much energy is used?','1.0 kWh',['0.6 kWh','1.5 kWh','60 kWh'],'40 minutes is 2/3 hour; energy=1.5×2/3=1.0 kWh.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','fractional-hour-energy','energy-metering','uses minutes as hours','1.5*(40/60)=1kWh'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-protection-relaying','A relay sees fault current flowing into its protected zone from either terminal. Which characteristic can support internal-fault discrimination?','Differential comparison of terminal currents',['Undervoltage only at one bus','A single fixed delay unrelated to current','A transformer tap position'],'Differential protection compares currents entering and leaving a zone and detects imbalance for internal faults.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','differential-zone-comparison','protection-zones','confuses an internal differential quantity with absolute load current',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-protection-relaying','A backup breaker is set to operate after the primary breaker for a downstream fault. What tradeoff does this provide?','Selectivity with delayed backup clearing if primary protection fails',['Faster clearing by every breaker simultaneously','No need for backup protection','Elimination of fault current'],'Time grading allows primary selectivity while retaining a backup path, with a clearing-time tradeoff.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','time-graded-backup','protection-coordination','expects backup and primary to trip together',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-protection-relaying','A ground fault current returns through an unintended parallel metallic path. What system issue should be investigated?','Bonding and grounding path integrity and current routing',['Only phase rotation','Transformer cooling class','Meter display resolution'],'Unintended parallel paths can carry current and create touch-voltage or protection concerns; trace bonding and return paths.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','ground-current-path','grounding-diagnosis','assumes all grounding conductors carry zero current in every condition',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-protection-relaying','A protective relay is tested with a secondary injection set. What does this test primarily verify?','Relay logic and response to injected signal values',['Primary conductor insulation condition by itself','Actual system fault level','Ground-grid step voltage'],'Secondary injection evaluates relay operation and settings, but does not alone prove the entire primary circuit and trip path.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','secondary-injection-scope','relay-testing','treats a relay test as end-to-end system verification',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-control-systems','A closed-loop system has steady-state error under a constant reference. Which change can reduce it for a type-0 unity-feedback system, subject to stability?','Adding suitable integral action',['Removing feedback','Reducing all sensor gain to zero','Adding only a pure delay'],'Integral action increases low-frequency loop gain and can eliminate constant-input steady-state error, while stability must be checked.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','integral-action-steady-error','controller-design','assumes more gain is always safe without stability review',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-control-systems','A sensor adds a constant bias to the measured output. What can a feedback controller mistakenly do?','Drive the true process away from target while correcting the biased measurement',['Ignore the sensor and remain exact','Remove the bias without calibration','Guarantee a stable true output'],'Feedback acts on measured error; a biased sensor can cause incorrect control action.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','sensor-bias-feedback','control-instrumentation','assumes feedback corrects sensor faults automatically',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-control-systems','A unity-feedback plant has open-loop transfer G(s)=K/s. What is the closed-loop transfer from reference to output?','K/(s+K)',['K/s','1/(s+K)','s/K'],'T=G/(1+G)=K/s ÷ (1+K/s)=K/(s+K).','D4','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','unity-feedback-closed-loop','control-model-reduction','forgets the feedback denominator','(K/s)/(1+K/s)=K/(s+K)'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-control-systems','A controller responds to the rate of change of error. Which action is this?','Derivative action',['Proportional action','Integral action','Reset-free deadband'],'Derivative action responds to error rate and can add damping but is sensitive to measurement noise.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','controller-action-identification','control-architecture','confuses error accumulation with error rate',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-power-electronics','An ideal full-wave rectifier is supplied by 60 Hz AC. What is the ripple repetition frequency before filtering?','120 Hz',['30 Hz','60 Hz','240 Hz'],'Full-wave rectification produces two output pulses per input cycle, giving 120 Hz.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','full-wave-ripple-frequency','rectifier-output','assumes only one pulse per AC cycle','2*60=120Hz'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-power-electronics','A buck converter’s output is lower than input in ideal continuous conduction. Which component stores energy during the switch-on interval?','Inductor',['Transformer core only','Fuse','Ground conductor'],'The inductor current rises and energy is stored in its magnetic field during the on interval.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','buck-inductor-energy','converter-operation','attributes energy storage to a protection component',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-power-electronics','A switching converter shows excessive output ripple after the load step. Which measurements help distinguish control response from inadequate energy storage?','Output waveform, inductor current, and control-loop response',['Case temperature only','Input wire color','Enclosure dimensions only'],'The transient waveform and inductor/control response reveal whether the issue is control bandwidth, current limit, or stored-energy capability.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','converter-load-step-diagnosis','power-electronic-transient','assumes ripple has a single cause',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-power-electronics','A single-phase inverter output is 230 V RMS sinusoidal. What is its approximate peak voltage?','325 V',['230 V','163 V','460 V'],'For a sine wave Vpeak=√2 Vrms≈1.414(230)=325 V.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','rms-to-peak-sinusoid','inverter-output','confuses RMS and peak values','sqrt(2)*230=325.3V'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-telecommunications','A 2 kHz sinusoid is sampled at 5 ksample/s without an adequate anti-alias filter. What concern applies?','It exceeds the Nyquist limit and can alias',['It is always represented exactly','Its frequency doubles by definition','Sampling eliminates all noise'],'A 2 kHz signal requires sampling above 4 ksample/s ideally; the actual anti-alias filter also matters.','D4','CONCEPTUAL_QUANTITATIVE','undersampling-alias-risk','data-acquisition','uses the Nyquist limit as equal to the signal frequency',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-telecommunications','A link budget has 10 dB transmit power and 3 dB cable loss, with all values in dB units. What power level remains before other losses?','7 dB',['13 dB','3.33 dB','−30 dB'],'Decibel gains and losses add algebraically: 10−3=7 dB.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','decibel-link-budget-sum','signal-path','multiplies decibel quantities as ordinary ratios','10-3=7dB'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-telecommunications','A communication receiver has adequate signal strength but poor intelligibility during interference. Which metric better represents signal relative to noise?','Signal-to-noise ratio',['Carrier frequency alone','Antenna color','Bit count in the display'],'SNR compares desired signal power with noise power and is relevant to detection quality.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','snr-quality-diagnostic','receiver-performance','equates received amplitude with signal quality',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-telecommunications','A link transmits 2,000 symbols/s using 4 distinct symbols. What is the ideal uncoded bit rate?','4,000 bit/s',['2,000 bit/s','8,000 bit/s','500 bit/s'],'Four symbols encode log₂4=2 bits each, so 2,000×2=4,000 bit/s.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','symbol-rate-bits-per-symbol','digital-link-capacity','equates baud and bit rate regardless of alphabet size','2000*log2(4)=4000bit/s'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-telecommunications','A receiver’s local oscillator drifts in frequency relative to the carrier. What impairment can result?','Carrier-frequency offset and degraded demodulation',['Higher conductor resistance','A guaranteed increase in bandwidth','Improved synchronization automatically'],'Frequency mismatch shifts the received spectrum and can impair coherent demodulation.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','carrier-frequency-offset','receiver-synchronization','confuses oscillator drift with channel bandwidth increase',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-computer-power-applications','A script computes feeder loading but omits units from a base-MVA conversion. What software safeguard is most useful?','Dimensional checks and explicit base metadata',['Suppress all warnings','Round every value to one digit','Reuse results from another case'],'Unit and base checks expose incompatible quantities before a plausible-looking result is accepted.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','per-unit-software-dimension-check','engineering-software-validation','assumes numeric type alone ensures physical validity',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-computer-power-applications','A power-system result is reproducible only when the software version, input case, and settings are retained. What practice is this?','Model and run provenance tracking',['Randomized input editing','Removing version labels','Manual result transcription only'],'Recording inputs, version, and settings makes engineering results traceable and reproducible.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','analysis-provenance','engineering-computation','treats an output value as independent of its input model',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-computer-power-applications','A numerical solver reports convergence but violates energy balance by a large margin. What is the best interpretation?','Numerical convergence alone does not establish a valid engineering solution',['The solution is necessarily correct','Energy conservation is irrelevant','Increase decimal places and accept it'],'Convergence is an algorithmic stopping condition; independent physical checks remain necessary.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','solver-convergence-versus-validity','simulation-verification','equates convergence with model validity',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-computer-power-applications','A data pipeline removes outliers before examining sensor status. What risk does this create?','A real fault signal may be discarded as an outlier',['It guarantees unbiased estimates','It creates more measurements','It verifies calibration'],'Outlier treatment should consider instrument state and engineering context so anomalous but real events are not erased.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','engineering-outlier-review','data-quality','assumes extreme observations are always noise',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-computer-power-applications','Two study cases produce different results after a software update. What is the first comparison?','Version, model assumptions, solver settings, and input data',['Only the screen layout','Only the user password','The number of charts'],'Controlled comparisons isolate changed software behavior from changed assumptions or inputs.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','software-version-regression','model-comparison','attributes a difference to the software without controlling inputs',''),
    ];
}

function b638_wave4_blueprints(): array
{
    return [
        // 25 Mathematics: integrative and interpretive, spread across smaller leaves.
        b638_q('b633-ree-math-complex-phasors','For z=6−j8, what is its principal angle?','−53.13° approximately',['53.13°','−36.87°','126.87°'],'The point is in quadrant IV; atan(8/6)=53.13°, with negative angle.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','complex-angle-quadrant','phasor-angle','ignores the imaginary sign when choosing quadrant','atan2(-8,6)=-53.13deg'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-math-complex-phasors','Two equal 5-unit phasors are separated by 120°. What is resultant magnitude?','5',['10','0','5√3'],'R=√(25+25+50cos120°)=5.','D4','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','phasor-resultant-cosine-law','phasor-combination','treats 120° separation as aligned vectors','sqrt(25+25+50*cos120deg)=5'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-math-complex-phasors','For a complex number z, what does z·z* represent?','The squared magnitude |z|²',['The angle of z','The conjugate of z','Twice its real part only'],'Multiplying by the conjugate yields a real nonnegative magnitude squared.','D3','CONCEPTUAL_QUANTITATIVE','complex-magnitude-squared','phasor-identity','confuses conjugate product with a phase operation',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-math-calculus-differential','A current decreases linearly from 8 A to 2 A over 3 s. What charge flows in that interval?','15 C',['18 C','10 C','6 C'],'For a linear ramp, average current is (8+2)/2=5 A; charge=5·3=15 C.','D4','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','linear-ramp-current-area','charge-integral','uses final current for the entire interval','((8+2)/2)*3=15C'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-math-calculus-differential','A differentiable response has derivative positive before t=2 and negative after t=2. What occurs at t=2?','A local maximum, if the response is continuous there',['A local minimum','A point of zero value','No extremum is possible'],'The slope changes from positive to negative, indicating a local maximum.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','first-derivative-sign-test','response-extremum','reverses the before/after slope signs',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-math-calculus-differential','A 4 F capacitor voltage rises at 0.5 V/s. What current enters its positive terminal?','2 A',['0.125 A','4.5 A','8 A'],'i=C dv/dt=4(0.5)=2 A using the passive sign convention.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','capacitor-current-capacitance-slope','charging-response','uses voltage divided by capacitance','4*.5=2A'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-math-probability-statistics','A component’s failure probability is 0.03 per independent mission. What is survival probability for one mission?','0.97',['0.03','0.30','1.03'],'Survival is the complement, 1−0.03=0.97.','D2','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','mission-survival-complement','reliability','reports failure probability as survival','1-.03=.97'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-math-probability-statistics','A scatterplot shows a curved relationship but near-zero Pearson correlation. What is the best interpretation?','The linear association is weak; a nonlinear relationship may still exist',['The variables are proven independent','There is no relationship','One variable cannot affect the other'],'Pearson correlation measures linear association and can miss curved dependence.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','correlation-nonlinearity-limit','data-interpretation','equates zero linear correlation with independence',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-math-discrete-economics','A 2,000 payment is due in two years at 5% annual discounting. What is its present worth?','1,814.06 approximately',['1,900','2,205','1,805'],'P=2000/(1.05)²≈1,814.06.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','single-payment-discount-two-period','capital-planning','uses a one-year discount factor','2000/1.05^2=1814.06'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-math-discrete-economics','An alternative has NPV=0 at the stated discount rate. What does that imply under the model?','Its discounted benefits equal discounted costs',['It has no cash flows','Its first cost is zero','It must have negative nominal return'],'Zero NPV is equality of present worth of benefits and costs at the specified rate.','D4','CONCEPTUAL_QUANTITATIVE','zero-npv-interpretation','investment-decision','mistakes zero NPV for zero project activity',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-math-discrete-economics','A device has initial cost 9,000 and salvage 1,000 after four years. Straight-line annual depreciation is what?','2,000',['2,250','1,000','8,000'],'(9,000−1,000)/4=2,000 per year.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','straight-line-depreciation-salvage','asset-life','depreciates full cost instead of depreciable basis','(9000-1000)/4=2000'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-math-trigonometry-analytic-geometry','A 15-unit vector has components 9 east and 12 north. What is its direction north of east?','53.13°',['36.87°','45°','126.87°'],'θ=atan(12/9)=53.13° measured from east toward north.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','vector-bearing-from-components','survey-vector','reverses the reference axis','atan(12/9)=53.13deg'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-math-trigonometry-analytic-geometry','For y=A cos(ωt+φ), what does increasing φ do when t=0 is fixed?','It shifts the phase at the origin',['It changes amplitude A only','It changes frequency ω only','It removes the periodicity'],'φ changes phase offset; A sets amplitude and ω sets angular frequency.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','sinusoidal-parameter-roles','waveform-model','confuses phase with frequency',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-math-trigonometry-analytic-geometry','A circle is centered at (2,−1) with radius 3. What is its equation?','(x−2)²+(y+1)²=9',['(x+2)²+(y−1)²=3','(x−2)+(y+1)=9','(x+2)²+(y+1)²=9'],'The center-radius form is (x−h)²+(y−k)²=r².','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','circle-center-radius-form','coordinate-model','reverses the signs in center coordinates','(x-2)^2+(y+1)^2=3^2=9'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-math-matrices-determinants','A square matrix maps every input to a unique output but different inputs can map to the same output. Is the map invertible?','No',['Yes, because outputs exist','Yes, for any square matrix','Only if its trace is positive'],'A many-to-one map is not injective and therefore has no inverse on its full domain.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','linear-map-injectivity','system-identifiability','assumes a square map is automatically invertible',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-math-matrices-determinants','Solve [[2,1],[1,1]][x,y]ᵀ=[5,3]ᵀ. What is x?','2',['1','3','5'],'The equations 2x+y=5 and x+y=3 give x=2.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','two-variable-system-solve','linear-model','subtracts right-hand sides but not left-hand sides','(5-3)=x=2'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-math-matrices-determinants','If A is orthogonal, what is AᵀA?','Identity matrix',['Zero matrix','A²','A+Aᵀ'],'Orthogonal matrices satisfy AᵀA=I, so their transpose is their inverse.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','orthogonality-invariant','coordinate-transform','confuses orthogonal columns with a zero product',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-math-sequences-series','A sampled signal has values 2, 6, 18,… . What is the next term under the same geometric rule?','54',['36','24','21'],'Each term is multiplied by 3, so the next is 18·3=54.','D2','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','geometric-sample-next-term','sampled-growth','continues by adding the previous difference','18*3=54'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-math-sequences-series','A geometric sequence has a₁=12 and a₄=1.5. What is its common ratio if positive?','0.5',['2','0.25','−0.5'],'12r³=1.5 gives r³=0.125 and r=0.5.','D4','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','geometric-ratio-from-separated-terms','decay-estimation','uses three steps as one step','(1.5/12)^(1/3)=.5'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-math-sequences-series','A recurrence adds a fixed positive increment. What is the shape of its term sequence versus index?','A straight-line arithmetic progression',['Geometric growth','Alternating signs necessarily','A constant sequence'],'A constant first difference produces an arithmetic progression linear in the index.','D3','CONCEPTUAL_QUANTITATIVE','recurrence-linear-growth','discrete-model','confuses fixed increment with fixed ratio',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-math-fourier-laplace','A unit impulse δ(t) has what Laplace transform?','1',['s','1/s','0'],'The transform of the unit impulse at zero is unity.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','impulse-transform-pair','system-excitation','confuses an impulse with a unit step',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-math-fourier-laplace','A stable first-order system has τ=0.25 s. What pole location corresponds to this time constant?','s=−4',['s=+4','s=−0.25','s=0'],'For a first-order mode e^(−t/τ), the pole is −1/τ=−4 s⁻¹.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','time-constant-to-pole','dynamic-model','uses τ instead of reciprocal and sign','-1/.25=-4'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-math-fourier-laplace','A signal is odd about zero and integrated over a symmetric interval. What is its integral?','Zero',['Twice its positive half','Its peak value','Always undefined'],'An odd integrable function cancels pairwise on a symmetric interval.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','odd-function-symmetric-integral','signal-symmetry','applies even-function doubling to an odd function',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-math-fourier-laplace','A system transfer function has numerator degree greater than denominator degree. What realization concern arises?','It may be improper and require ideal differentiation or be noncausal in standard finite-dimensional form',['It is always stable','It must have zero gain','It contains no dynamics'],'A proper causal transfer function ordinarily has numerator degree no greater than denominator degree.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','transfer-function-properness','model-validity','equates high numerator degree with stability',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-math-fourier-laplace','A Fourier waveform has half-wave symmetry f(t+T/2)=−f(t). Which harmonics vanish?','Even harmonics and DC',['All odd harmonics','Only the fundamental','No harmonics'],'Half-wave symmetry cancels the DC and even harmonics while allowing odd harmonics.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','half-wave-symmetry-harmonics','spectrum-analysis','reverses odd/even harmonic selection',''),
        // 30 Allied: physical interpretation, measurements, safety, contracts, and computing.
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-mechanics','A 50 N force moves a body 4 m in its direction. What work is done?','200 J',['12.5 J','54 J','0 J'],'W=Fs=50·4=200 J for aligned force and displacement.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','aligned-force-work','energy-transfer','divides force by displacement','50*4=200J'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-mechanics','A 3 kg cart moving at 4 m/s stops. What impulse magnitude acts?','12 N·s',['7 N·s','24 N·s','1.33 N·s'],'Impulse equals momentum change: |0−3·4|=12 kg·m/s.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','momentum-impulse-change','braking-event','uses kinetic energy instead of momentum','3*4=12Ns'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-mechanics','A body is in static equilibrium. Which pair of conditions is required for a rigid body?','Zero resultant force and zero resultant moment',['Zero velocity only','Equal mass and volume','Zero force but arbitrary moment'],'Static rigid-body equilibrium requires both translational and rotational balance.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','rigid-body-equilibrium-pair','support-check','checks force balance but omits moment balance',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-materials','A tensile coupon has original area 50 mm² and carries 5 kN. What nominal stress is applied?','100 MPa',['10 MPa','250 MPa','0.01 MPa'],'5,000 N/50 mm²=100 N/mm²=100 MPa.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','tensile-stress-nominal','material-test','converts kN incorrectly','5000/50=100MPa'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-materials','A high-strength alloy has lower fracture toughness than a lower-strength alternative. What risk should be considered?','Crack-like flaws may propagate at lower energy absorption',['Higher strength guarantees higher toughness','The material cannot fracture','Only density changes'],'Strength and fracture toughness are distinct properties; flaw sensitivity matters.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','strength-toughness-distinction','material-selection','treats high yield strength as proof of crack tolerance',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-materials','A constrained metal member is heated. Why can thermal stress develop?','Expansion is restrained, preventing free thermal strain',['Heating eliminates all strain','The elastic modulus becomes zero necessarily','Mass is converted to force'],'A temperature change tends to create strain; restraint converts part of that tendency into stress.','D4','CONCEPTUAL_QUANTITATIVE','restrained-thermal-strain','installation-stress','assumes only external mechanical loads create stress',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-thermodynamics','A heat pump delivers 5 kW while consuming 1.25 kW. What is COP heating?','4',['0.25','3.75','6.25'],'COPH=QH/Win=5/1.25=4.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','heat-pump-performance-ratio','building-thermal','subtracts work from delivered heat before forming COP','5/1.25=4'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-thermodynamics','A process is adiabatic. Which statement is guaranteed by the definition?','No heat crosses the system boundary',['Temperature is constant','Work is zero','Internal energy is constant'],'Adiabatic means Q=0; temperature and internal energy may still change due to work.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','adiabatic-boundary-definition','process-model','equates no heat transfer with no temperature change',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-thermodynamics','A 2 kg body cools by 5 K with c=900 J/(kg·K). How much heat magnitude is released?','9 kJ',['1.8 kJ','4.5 kJ','18 kJ'],'|Q|=mc|ΔT|=2·900·5=9,000 J.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','cooling-sensible-heat','thermal-release','drops the temperature interval','2*900*5=9000J'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-fluid-mechanics','A fluid has specific gravity 0.8 relative to water at 1,000 kg/m³. What is its density?','800 kg/m³',['1,250 kg/m³','80 kg/m³','0.8 kg/m³'],'Specific gravity times reference density gives 0.8·1,000=800 kg/m³.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','specific-gravity-density','fluid-identification','treats relative density as density units','0.8*1000=800kg/m^3'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-fluid-mechanics','A pump’s discharge pressure is high but delivered flow is nearly zero. What operational issue should be checked?','A closed valve, blockage, or operation near shutoff condition',['That continuity is violated','That fluid density is negative','Only the pipe color'],'High head with little flow can occur at shutoff or blockage; inspect system state and pump operating limits.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','pump-shutoff-diagnosis','hydraulic-operation','assumes pressure alone proves useful flow delivery',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-fluid-mechanics','A 0.03 m³/s flow passes through an area of 0.015 m². What is mean velocity?','2 m/s',['0.5 m/s','0.0005 m/s','45 m/s'],'v=Q/A=0.03/0.015=2 m/s.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','flow-area-velocity','conduit-measurement','uses A/Q instead of Q/A','0.03/.015=2m/s'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-electronics-semiconductor','A BJT base-emitter junction is reverse biased beyond its ordinary operating condition. What is the design implication?','It may exceed a low reverse-voltage rating and be damaged',['It automatically enters normal forward active operation','Its gain becomes infinite','It is protected by the collector load'],'The base-emitter junction commonly has limited reverse breakdown capability; respect device ratings.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','bjt-base-emitter-reverse-rating','device-protection','assumes transistor junctions tolerate arbitrary reverse voltage',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-electronics-semiconductor','A MOSFET gate capacitance is charged from 0 to 10 V by 20 nC. What is the approximate capacitance?','2 nF',['0.5 nF','200 nF','20 nF'],'C=Q/V=20 nC/10 V=2 nF.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','gate-charge-capacitance','switching-drive','multiplies charge and voltage','20e-9/10=2nF'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-electronics-semiconductor','A transistor is biased at cutoff in a switching circuit. What is its ideal collector current?','Approximately zero',['Maximum rated current','Equal to base current','Infinite'],'Cutoff turns the device off in the ideal switch model.','D2','CONCEPTUAL_QUANTITATIVE','transistor-cutoff-state','switch-operation','confuses cutoff with saturation',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-electronics-analog','An inverting amplifier has Rin=5 kΩ and Rf=20 kΩ. What is output for +0.2 V input in the ideal model?','−0.8 V',['+0.8 V','−0.05 V','+4 V'],'Gain=−Rf/Rin=−4, so output=−4(0.2)=−0.8 V.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','inverting-stage-input-output','signal-conditioning','omits inversion or uses the resistor ratio backward','-(20/5)*.2=-.8V'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-electronics-analog','An amplifier’s gain falls at high frequency because of internal poles. What general behavior is this?','Finite bandwidth',['Infinite slew rate','Perfect frequency independence','Zero phase shift at all frequencies'],'Real amplifier gain and phase vary with frequency due to finite bandwidth and poles.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','amplifier-bandwidth-limit','frequency-response','assumes an ideal op-amp model applies at all frequencies',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-electronics-digital','A 10-bit ADC reports code 512 on a 0–5 V ideal span with 1024 codes. What input is indicated approximately?','2.5 V',['5 V','0.5 V','1.25 V'],'512/1024 of the full span is approximately 2.5 V under the given scaling convention.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','adc-code-to-voltage','digitized-measurement','uses code as volts directly','512/1024*5=2.5V'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-electronics-digital','A synchronous counter’s output changes only on a clock edge. What does synchronous mean here?','State elements share a common timing reference',['Every gate has a different random clock','No memory is present','The output is analog'],'Synchronous state changes are coordinated by a shared clocking event.','D2','NON_NUMERICAL','synchronous-state-update','digital-timing','confuses clocked logic with combinational logic',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-instrumentation','A current sensor output is noisy only when a nearby motor switches. Which coupling should be investigated?','Electromagnetic interference and grounding/layout paths',['Sensor span alone','The number of display digits','The file name'],'Switching transients can couple through fields, common impedance, or cabling and affect measurement.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','switching-emi-measurement','instrument-noise','assumes sensor noise must be intrinsic to the sensor',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-instrumentation','A calibrated instrument reads 100.8 units for a 100.0-unit reference. What signed error is observed?','+0.8 units',['−0.8 units','0.8% without calculation','100.8 units'],'Signed error=indication−reference=100.8−100.0=+0.8.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','signed-indication-error','calibration-check','reverses reference and indication','100.8-100=.8'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-safety-code','An electrically isolated conductor is returned to service. What must precede energization?','Clear personnel and tools, restore guards, and communicate the controlled re-energization',['Remove the lock without coordination','Assume everyone has left','Energize while inspection continues'],'Re-energization requires controlled release of isolation after personnel and equipment are clear.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','controlled-reenergization','isolation-release','treats completion of repair as proof the area is clear',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-safety-code','A protective device trips repeatedly after a fault. What is the safe response?','Investigate and correct the cause; do not repeatedly reset without assessment',['Oversize it immediately','Hold it closed','Bypass it to restore service'],'Repeated trips indicate a condition requiring diagnosis; bypassing protection can expose people and equipment to danger.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','repeated-trip-diagnosis','protective-device-safety','treats protective operation as a nuisance rather than evidence',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-chemistry','A gas occupies 2 L at 100 kPa. At constant temperature, what volume is predicted at 200 kPa?','1 L',['4 L','2 L','0.5 L'],'Boyle’s relation gives P₁V₁=P₂V₂, so V₂=100·2/200=1 L.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','boyle-law-volume-pressure','gas-property','assumes volume rises with pressure at fixed temperature','100*2/200=1L'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-chemistry','A corrosion process is electrochemical. Which condition can accelerate it?','A conductive electrolyte bridging anodic and cathodic regions',['Perfectly dry isolation in all cases','Removal of every potential difference','A chemically inert sealed environment'],'Electrolyte and electrochemical potential differences support corrosion current.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','corrosion-electrolyte-path','material-durability','treats corrosion as unrelated to ionic conduction',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-law-code-ethics','An engineer receives confidential project data unrelated to the engineer’s authorized role. What is appropriate?','Protect it and use or disclose it only as authorized or required by duty/law',['Publish it for convenience','Forward it to a competitor','Assume public availability'],'Professional confidentiality requires proper handling, subject to applicable legal and public-safety obligations.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','confidential-information-duty','professional-practice','treats access as permission to disclose',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-law-code-ethics','An engineer’s seal is requested on work the engineer did not review. What is the proper response?','Do not authenticate work without the required responsible review',['Sign to meet the deadline','Let an assistant use the seal','Sign if another engineer requested it'],'Professional authentication should reflect responsible charge and an adequate basis under controlling rules.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','responsible-authentication','professional-licensure','equates request from a colleague with technical responsibility',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-contracts-specifications','A bid proposes a lower-cost component with a shorter warranty but otherwise meets the listed ratings. What should the evaluation do?','Compare all contractual and lifecycle requirements and document any variance',['Select solely by price','Ignore the warranty','Assume warranty is never relevant'],'Evaluation should follow stated criteria and identify lifecycle or contractual deviations transparently.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','bid-equivalence-lifecycle-review','procurement-evaluation','reduces technical procurement to first cost only',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-contracts-specifications','A commissioning test fails the stated acceptance criterion. What is the next step?','Document the result, assess cause, and follow the contract’s corrective/retest process',['Change the criterion after seeing the result','Delete the test record','Declare acceptance without approval'],'Acceptance criteria and nonconformance handling should be followed and traceably resolved.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','commissioning-nonconformance','acceptance-testing','alters criteria retroactively to pass a result',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-computer-programming','A fixed-width signed addition overflows its representable range. What should robust code do?','Detect or safely handle overflow according to the application',['Wrap silently in every safety-critical calculation','Assume the result is exact','Delete the sign bit'],'Overflow can invalidate numerical results and should be handled explicitly.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','integer-overflow-handling','embedded-arithmetic','treats modular wraparound as physically meaningful without validation',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-computer-programming','A sensor message includes a checksum that fails. What should the receiver do?','Reject or flag the corrupted message and follow the defined fault response',['Use the value as valid','Change the checksum to match','Ignore data quality'],'A failed integrity check means the received payload cannot be trusted as intact.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','message-integrity-failure','telemetry-validation','treats a detected communication error as valid measurement',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-allied-computer-programming','A software test passes on nominal inputs but fails at zero and maximum values. Which test set is missing?','Boundary and limit-condition tests',['Only performance tests','A user-interface color review','A test with the same nominal value repeated'],'Boundary tests probe edge cases where indexing, overflow, and physical limits often expose defects.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','boundary-value-testing','software-verification','assumes nominal-case success generalizes to limits',''),
        // 45 Professional: application across machines, power, protection, controls and communications.
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-generators-conversion','A synchronous generator is at 1,500 rpm with 4 poles. What is electrical frequency?','50 Hz',['25 Hz','100 Hz','60 Hz'],'f=PN/120=4·1500/120=50 Hz.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','speed-pole-frequency','generator-rating','uses pole pairs without the 120 conversion','4*1500/120=50Hz'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-generators-conversion','A generator’s real-power output rises on an isolated bus. What control normally supplies the added energy?','Prime-mover governor/input',['Excitation system only','Transformer tap alone','Grounding electrode'],'Mechanical input must rise to supply increased real electrical output plus losses.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','islanded-real-power-governor','generator-load-sharing','assigns real-power control to excitation',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-generators-conversion','A 50 kW shaft input yields 45 kW electrical output. What is the loss?','5 kW',['45 kW','95 kW','0.9 kW'],'Loss=input−output=50−45=5 kW.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','generator-loss-balance','machine-efficiency','reports efficiency as loss','50-45=5kW'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-generators-conversion','Two alternators are to be paralleled. Which condition is essential before closing the tie?','Compatible voltage, frequency, phase sequence, and phase angle',['Equal prime-mover fuel only','Identical frame color','Zero field current'],'Synchronizing requires matching electrical conditions to avoid severe transient currents and torque.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','alternator-synchronizing-conditions','parallel-operation','confuses mechanical similarity with electrical synchronism',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-generators-conversion','A generator uses 400 kJ of mechanical energy to deliver 340 kJ electrically. What is efficiency?','85%',['60%','117.6%','15%'],'η=340/400=0.85=85%.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','energy-efficiency-ratio','conversion-efficiency','divides loss by input and calls it efficiency','340/400=85%'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-power-analysis','A three-phase bus has 13.8 kV line voltage and 20 MVA load. What is line current at unity power factor?','0.837 kA approximately',['1.45 kA','0.484 kA','13.8 kA'],'I=S/(√3V)=20 MVA/(√3·13.8 kV)≈0.837 kA.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','three-phase-current-from-mva','system-loading','omits the three-phase √3 factor','20e6/(sqrt(3)*13.8e3)=0.837kA'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-power-analysis','A fault study assumes zero fault impedance. What case is being approximated?','A bolted fault',['An open circuit','A normal load','A high-impedance fault'],'A bolted fault is a short-circuit approximation with negligible fault impedance.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','bolted-fault-assumption','short-circuit-model','uses zero impedance to mean open circuit',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-power-analysis','A network’s short-circuit level is reported in MVA. What does this quantity broadly represent?','Fault apparent power at the specified voltage and fault current',['Annual energy consumption','Real losses over a year','Transformer efficiency'],'Short-circuit MVA relates nominal voltage to prospective fault current; it is not annual energy.','D3','CONCEPTUAL_QUANTITATIVE','short-circuit-mva-meaning','fault-level-interpretation','confuses fault capacity with energy use',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-power-analysis','A load-flow case shows negative generation at a bus whose injection convention is positive. What should be reviewed?','Sign convention and whether the bus is modeled as net load',['Only line resistance','The title of the case','Whether the bus is physically above ground'],'Negative injection can represent net consumption under the stated convention; verify model semantics.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','bus-injection-sign','power-flow-interpretation','assumes a negative number must be a software failure',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-power-analysis','A 3-phase load absorbs 12 MW at 0.8 lagging power factor. What reactive power magnitude applies?','9 MVAr',['15 MVAr','7.2 MVAr','3 MVAr'],'tanφ=0.75, so Q=P tanφ=12·0.75=9 MVAr.','D4','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','three-phase-reactive-power-from-pf','power-flow-input','uses apparent power as reactive power','12*tan(acos(.8))=9MVAr'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-transmission-distribution','A feeder’s receiving voltage is lower under load than at its source. Which effects can contribute?','Series impedance and load current, with reactive effects included',['Only conductor color','An increase in system frequency','A larger transformer pole count'],'Voltage drop depends on current and network impedance and can include reactive power effects.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','feeder-voltage-drop-causes','distribution-voltage','attributes voltage drop to resistance alone in all cases',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-transmission-distribution','A 3-phase feeder carries 100 A at 0.9 power factor and 400 V line-to-line. What real power is delivered ideally?','62.4 kW approximately',['36 kW','69.3 kW','40 kW'],'P=√3 VLI pf=√3·400·100·0.9≈62.4 kW.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','three-phase-real-power','feeder-load','omits power factor or phase factor','sqrt(3)*400*100*.9=62.35kW'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-transmission-distribution','A feeder load is moved closer to the substation while total load stays the same. What loss trend is generally expected?','Lower current-related line loss on the shortened loaded section may result',['Loss must increase','Loss is unchanged under every topology','Frequency changes proportionally'],'Reducing the length carrying the same load can reduce resistance and I²R loss, all else equal.','D4','CONCEPTUAL_QUANTITATIVE','feeder-length-loss-trend','distribution-planning','assumes load relocation cannot change network losses',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-transmission-distribution','A transformer tap is changed to raise a downstream voltage. What should be checked after the change?','Voltage at other buses, equipment limits, and reactive/operating impacts',['Only the tap label','That every voltage rises equally','Nothing if one bus improves'],'A tap change affects the network and must be checked across relevant buses and operating constraints.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','tap-change-system-impact','voltage-control','optimizes one bus without checking the rest of the system',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-transmission-distribution','A line has 0.2 pu reactance on a 100 MVA base. What is its reactance on a 50 MVA base at unchanged voltage base?','0.1 pu',['0.4 pu','0.2 pu','0.05 pu'],'Zpu,new=Zpu,old(Snew/Sold) at unchanged voltage base, so 0.2·50/100=0.1 pu.','D4','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','per-unit-impedance-base-change','base-conversion','uses the inverse base ratio','0.2*50/100=.1pu'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-transmission-distribution','A distribution circuit experiences a peak during a short interval but low annual use. Which metric captures annual average relative to peak?','Load factor',['Power factor','Diversity factor by itself','Voltage regulation'],'Load factor is average demand divided by peak demand over the same period.','D3','NON_NUMERICAL','load-factor-definition','demand-characterization','confuses load factor with power factor',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-wiring-utilization','A 3-phase balanced load is rated 30 kW at 400 V and unity power factor. What line current is estimated?','43.3 A approximately',['75 A','25 A','17.3 A'],'I=P/(√3V pf)=30,000/(√3·400)≈43.3 A.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','three-phase-current-from-kw','load-sizing','uses single-phase V instead of the three-phase relation','30000/(sqrt(3)*400)=43.3A'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-wiring-utilization','A motor’s measured power factor is low at light load. What is a plausible reason?','Magnetizing current remains while real load current is small',['The motor has no reactive current','The voltage must be zero','The power factor is independent of loading'],'Magnetizing current is comparatively significant when the motor is lightly loaded, lowering power factor.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','motor-light-load-power-factor','motor-efficiency','assumes power factor is fixed by nameplate alone',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-wiring-utilization','A balanced 3-phase load consumes 12 kWh over 2 hours. What is its average real power?','6 kW',['24 kW','12 kW','0.167 kW'],'Average power=energy/time=12/2=6 kW.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','energy-to-average-power','load-profile','multiplies energy by time','12/2=6kW'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-wiring-utilization','A luminaire has good efficiency but poor task visibility due to shadowing. What should be redesigned?','Fixture placement and distribution relative to the work plane',['Only its nameplate wattage','The transformer frequency','The conductor insulation class'],'Illumination quality depends on spatial distribution and obstructions, not efficacy alone.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','task-plane-shadowing','lighting-layout','equates source efficacy with task-plane performance',''),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-wiring-utilization','A load is 5 kVA at 0.6 lagging power factor. What real power is used?','3 kW',['8.33 kW','5 kW','2 kW'],'P=S·pf=5(0.6)=3 kW.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','apparent-to-real-power','load-accounting','divides apparent power by the power factor','5*.6=3kW'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-protection-relaying','A current transformer ratio is 400:5. What secondary current corresponds to 240 A primary current?','3 A',['48 A','6 A','0.3 A'],'The ratio is 80:1, so secondary current is 240/80=3 A.','D3','CALCULATION_REQUIRED','ct-ratio-scaling','protection-measurement','uses the stated ratio backward','240*(5/400)=3A'),
        b638_q('b633-ree-pro-protection-relaying','A relay trips for an external fault through a transformer. Which issue should be investigated?','CT ratio/polarity compensation and restraint behavior',['Only the breaker paint','The normal power factor alone','Whether the fault is downstream of every device'],'External through-fault stability depends on correct CT compensation and relay restraint.','D4','NON_NUMERICAL','transformer-differential-through-fault','relay-stability','assumes differential protection should trip on every external fault',''),
